module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SelfBraidingInvertible.Algebra
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertiblePullback.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionRingGeometric.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.InvertibleSummandSheafify

/-!
# An invertible sheaf of modules has trivial self-braiding

Let `𝒪` be a sheaf of commutative rings on an arbitrary site `(C, J)` and let `L` be an
invertible sheaf of `𝒪`-modules in the sense of Stacks Tag 01CS. This file proves that the
braiding of `L` with itself is the identity,
`Stacks.GradedSections.HasTrivialSelfBraiding L`, which is the hypothesis the coherence of the
multiplication on the tensor powers of `L` (Stacks Tag 01CU) requires.

**The statement is not formal.** In a general symmetric monoidal category an invertible object
satisfies only `β ≫ β = 𝟙`; the odd line in super vector spaces is invertible with
self-braiding `-𝟙`. So something about sheaves of modules has to be used, and the route through
local triviality — the one
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/SectionRingGeometric/Basic.lean` takes on a ringed space whose
stalks are local rings — is *not available here*: on a one-object site with `𝒪 = R` a Dedekind
domain of nontrivial class group, an invertible sheaf of modules is a nontrivial invertible
`R`-module, which is not cyclic and has no nontrivial covering to become cyclic on.

## The argument

Write `ψ : L ⊗ N ⟶ 𝒪` for the locally bijective pairing of presheaves of modules which
invertibility supplies (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_locallyBijective_pairing`, Tag 0B8N (b)).

1. **The exchange morphism.** The two ways of contracting `ψ` against a third factor of `L`,
   `pairLeft ψ : (x ⊗ y) ⊗ v ↦ ψ (x ⊗ y) • v` and `pairRight ψ : (x ⊗ y) ⊗ v ↦ ψ (v ⊗ y) • x`,
   are *not* equal — their difference is precisely the self-braiding scalar. But `pairLeft ψ` is
   again locally bijective (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.W_whiskerRight`: the local
   isomorphisms are stable under tensoring), so by the universal property of a locally bijective
   map into a sheaf (`PresheafOfModules.homEquivOfIsLocallyBijective`) there is a *unique*
   `g : L ⟶ L` with `pairLeft ψ ≫ g = pairRight ψ`. On sections that reads
   `ψ (x ⊗ y) • g v = ψ (v ⊗ y) • x`, which is `exists_exchange`.
2. **Rank-one witnesses.** On the covering sieve of an object where `1` lies in the image of
   `ψ`, write `1 = ∑ j, ψ (x j ⊗ y j)`. Reading the exchange identity with `x := v` and
   `v := x j` gives `ψ (v ⊗ y j) • g (x j) = ψ (x j ⊗ y j) • v` for *every* section `v`: so
   multiplying by the scalar `c j = ψ (x j ⊗ y j)` carries all of `L` into the cyclic submodule
   generated by the single element `g (x j)`.
3. **The algebra.** `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.tmul_comm_of_rankOne` turns those witnesses
   into symmetry of the tensor square: the scalars `c j` do not annihilate
   `v ⊗ₜ w - w ⊗ₜ v`, but their *squares* do, and a family of scalars summing to `1` whose
   squares annihilate an element annihilates it, by the radical of its annihilator ideal.
4. **Sheafification.** The braiding of presheaves of modules is sectionwise the transposition of
   a tensor square, so it agrees with the identity after the sheafification unit on a covering
   sieve of every object; the target is a sheaf, hence separated. The three transport lemmas of
   the sibling file — `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.map_eq_of_unit_comp_eq`,
   `braiding_eq_id_of_localization` and `braiding_eq_id_of_iso` — carry that to the braiding on
   `SheafOfModules` itself.

Only step 4 is shared with the ringed-space file; steps 1–3 replace its geometric input.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.pairLeft` and `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.pairRight`: the two
  contractions of a pairing `L ⊗ N ⟶ 𝒪` against a third factor of `L`.
* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.pairHom`: a pairing read as an additive map into the structure
  presheaf, so that its values can be summed there.
* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.HasLocallySymmetricSquare`: a presheaf of modules whose tensor
  square is symmetric on a covering sieve of every object. This is strictly weaker than
  `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.IsLocallyCyclic`, and it is all the sheafification step consumes.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.exists_exchange`: **the exchange morphism.**
* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.tmul_comm_of_dualBasis`: a dual basis for a locally bijective
  pairing over one object makes the tensor square of the sections over that object symmetric.
* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.hasLocallySymmetricSquare_of_isInvertible`: **an invertible
  sheaf of modules has locally symmetric tensor square**, on any site.
* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.braiding_eq_id_of_locallySymmetric`: a sheaf of modules with
  locally symmetric tensor square has trivial self-braiding.
* `Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.hasTrivialSelfBraiding`: **`β_ L L = 𝟙` for an invertible sheaf
  of modules**, as the instance that the coherence of the tensor-power multiplication asks for.

## Implementation notes

**No slice site.** The obvious way to produce the element `g (x j)` of step 2 is to restrict to
the slice site over the covering object, where the local sections `x j` become global and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isSplitMono_of_dualBasis` applies. That route costs the extra hypothesis
`∀ V, (J.over V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat`, which Mathlib does not derive from the
hypothesis on `J` (see `Mathlib/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/Quasicoherent.lean`, where it is
assumed) and which the consumers of this instance do not have. Applying the universal property to
`pairLeft ψ`, whose source carries the third factor, avoids it: the needed element is
`g` applied to a *local* section, and `g` is a global morphism.

**Transparency.** `↑((𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing 𝒪)).obj U)` and
`↑((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U)` are equal only at
default transparency, and `•` elaborates through `binop%`, which looks past a type ascription;
so `ψ.app U z • v` does not elaborate and `(ψ.app U z : _) • v` does not either. Every statement
below therefore either takes the scalar as a separate argument with an equation naming it — the
pattern of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.coev_proj_app` — or goes through `pairHom`. For the same reason
the element-level steps are `rfl`-chains closed by `rw` on those equations, never `rw` through a
tensor of presheaves: `rw` works at implicit transparency and reports the mismatch as a failure
to find the pattern.

**The scalars are summed in the structure presheaf, not in the monoidal unit.** `pairHom` exists
exactly so that `∑ j, ψ (x j ⊗ y j) = 1` is a statement about `𝒪`, where
`Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible.tmul_comm_of_rankOne` can consume it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8N)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Category Limits Opposite MonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification
open scoped TensorProduct

universe v u w

namespace Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{w}}

/-! ### The two contractions of a pairing against a third factor -/

section Exchange

variable {Lp Np : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪}

/-- A pairing `L ⊗ N ⟶ 𝒪`, read as an additive map into the structure presheaf. The values of a
pairing live in the monoidal unit, whose ring of sections is the structure presheaf only up to
default transparency; this records the identification once so that the values can be added and
summed in `𝒪`. -/
noncomputable def pairHom (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)) (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (Lp ⊗ Np).obj U →+ (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U where
  toFun z := ψ.app U z
  map_zero' := map_zero _
  map_add' z z' := map_add _ z z'

/-- Contraction of a pairing on the first two factors of `(L ⊗ N) ⊗ L`: on sections,
`(x ⊗ y) ⊗ v ↦ ψ (x ⊗ y) • v`. -/
noncomputable def pairLeft (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)) :
    (Lp ⊗ Np) ⊗ Lp ⟶ Lp :=
  (ψ ▷ Lp) ≫ (λ_ Lp).hom

/-- Contraction of a pairing on the last two factors of `(L ⊗ N) ⊗ L`: on sections,
`(x ⊗ y) ⊗ v ↦ ψ (v ⊗ y) • x`. The two factors of `L` are exchanged by the braiding of `N` past
`L`, never by the self-braiding of `L`, which is what is to be computed. -/
noncomputable def pairRight (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)) :
    (Lp ⊗ Np) ⊗ Lp ⟶ Lp :=
  (α_ Lp Np Lp).hom ≫ (Lp ◁ (β_ Np Lp).hom) ≫ (Lp ◁ ψ) ≫ (ρ_ Lp).hom

/-- On sections, `pairLeft ψ` sends `(x ⊗ y) ⊗ v` to `r • v`, where `r = ψ (x ⊗ y)`. -/
lemma pairLeft_app (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x : Lp.obj U) (y : Np.obj U) (v : Lp.obj U) (r : (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U)
    (hr : ψ.app U (x ⊗ₜ y) = r) :
    (pairLeft ψ).app U ((x ⊗ₜ y) ⊗ₜ v) = r • v := by
  have h1 : (pairLeft ψ).app U ((x ⊗ₜ y) ⊗ₜ v)
      = (λ_ (Lp.obj U)).hom (ψ.app U (x ⊗ₜ y) ⊗ₜ v) := rfl
  rw [h1, hr, ModuleCat.MonoidalCategory.leftUnitor_hom_apply]

/-- On sections, `pairRight ψ` sends `(x ⊗ y) ⊗ v` to `s • x`, where `s = ψ (v ⊗ y)`. -/
lemma pairRight_app (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪)) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (x : Lp.obj U) (y : Np.obj U) (v : Lp.obj U) (s : (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U)
    (hs : ψ.app U (v ⊗ₜ y) = s) :
    (pairRight ψ).app U ((x ⊗ₜ y) ⊗ₜ v) = s • x := by
  have h1 : (pairRight ψ).app U ((x ⊗ₜ y) ⊗ₜ v)
      = (ρ_ (Lp.obj U)).hom (x ⊗ₜ ψ.app U (v ⊗ₜ y)) := rfl
  rw [h1, hs, ModuleCat.MonoidalCategory.rightUnitor_hom_apply]

variable [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **The exchange morphism of a locally bijective pairing.** Contracting `ψ` against the third
factor of `(L ⊗ N) ⊗ L` on the left and on the right gives two morphisms to `L`; the left one is
again locally bijective, so the right one factors uniquely through it, by a morphism
`g : L ⟶ L`. On sections the factorisation says `ψ (x ⊗ y) • g v = ψ (v ⊗ y) • x`: the exchange
of the two factors of `L` in the pairing, corrected by `g`.

Local bijectivity of `pairLeft ψ` is stability of the local isomorphisms under tensoring,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.W_whiskerRight`, which is where the sheaf condition on
the site enters. -/
theorem exists_exchange {Lp Np : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪}
    (hLp : Presheaf.IsSheaf J Lp.presheaf)
    (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪))
    [PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J ψ]
    [PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective J ψ] :
    ∃ g : Lp ⟶ Lp, ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (x v : Lp.obj U) (y : Np.obj U)
      (r s : (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U),
      ψ.app U (x ⊗ₜ y) = r → ψ.app U (v ⊗ₜ y) = s → r • g.app U v = s • x := by
  have hW : J.W ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪)).map ψ) :=
    J.W_of_isLocallyBijective _
  have hW2 : J.W ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪)).map (pairLeft ψ)) := by
    rw [show pairLeft ψ = (ψ ▷ Lp) ≫ (λ_ Lp).hom from rfl, Functor.map_comp]
    exact J.W.comp_mem _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.W_whiskerRight 𝒪 ψ Lp hW)
      (J.W.of_isIso _)
  have : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective J (pairLeft ψ) := hW2.isLocallyInjective
  have : PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J (pairLeft ψ) := hW2.isLocallySurjective
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ : ∃ g, pairLeft ψ ≫ g = pairRight ψ :=
    ⟨(PresheafOfModules.homEquivOfIsLocallyBijective (pairLeft ψ) hLp).symm (pairRight ψ),
      (PresheafOfModules.homEquivOfIsLocallyBijective (pairLeft ψ) hLp).apply_symm_apply _⟩
  refine ⟨g, fun U x v y r s hr hs ↦ ?_⟩
  have hlin : g.app U (r • v) = r • g.app U v := map_smul _ r v
  have e1 : (pairLeft ψ ≫ g).app U ((x ⊗ₜ y) ⊗ₜ v) = g.app U (r • v) :=
    congrArg (fun z ↦ g.app U z) (pairLeft_app ψ U x y v r hr)
  rw [← hlin, ← e1, hg, pairRight_app ψ U x y v s hs]

/-- **A dual basis over one object makes the tensor square of the sections symmetric.** Finitely
many sections `x j` of `L` and `y j` of `N` whose pairings sum to `1` give, through the exchange
morphism, rank-one witnesses for the module of sections of `L`: multiplying by
`c j = ψ (x j ⊗ y j)` carries every section into the cyclic submodule generated by `g (x j)`, and
the `c j` sum to `1`. -/
theorem tmul_comm_of_dualBasis {Lp Np : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪}
    (hLp : Presheaf.IsSheaf J Lp.presheaf)
    (ψ : Lp ⊗ Np ⟶ 𝟙_ (PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪))
    [PresheafOfModules.IsLocallySurjective J ψ]
    [PresheafOfModules.IsLocallyInjective J ψ]
    (U : Cᵒᵖ) {n : ℕ} (x : Fin n → Lp.obj U) (y : Fin n → Np.obj U)
    (hsum : ∑ j, pairHom ψ U (x j ⊗ₜ y j) = 1) (a b : Lp.obj U) :
    a ⊗ₜ[(structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U] b = b ⊗ₜ[(structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U] a := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_exchange hLp ψ
  refine tmul_comm_of_rankOne (R := (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U)
    (fun j v ↦ pairHom ψ U (v ⊗ₜ y j)) (fun j ↦ g.app U (x j))
    (fun j ↦ pairHom ψ U (x j ⊗ₜ y j)) hsum (fun j v ↦ ?_) a b
  exact hg U v (x j) (y j) _ _ rfl rfl

end Exchange

/-! ### Invertible sheaves of modules have locally symmetric tensor square -/

variable (𝒪) in
/-- A presheaf of modules is **locally symmetric** when its module of sections has symmetric
tensor square over every object of a covering sieve of every object of the site. This is weaker
than `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.IsLocallyCyclic` — a cyclic module of sections has symmetric
tensor square, but an invertible sheaf of modules on a general site is nowhere locally cyclic —
and it is all the sheafification step below consumes. -/
def HasLocallySymmetricSquare (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪) : Prop :=
  ∀ U : C, ∃ S : Sieve U, S ∈ J U ∧ ∀ ⦃Y : C⦄ (f : Y ⟶ U), S f →
    ∀ a b : P.obj (op Y),
      a ⊗ₜ[(structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj (op Y)] b
        = b ⊗ₜ[(structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj (op Y)] a

/-- **An invertible sheaf of modules has locally symmetric tensor square**, on an arbitrary site.
The covering sieve of an object `U` is the one on which the unit section of `𝒪` lies in the image
of the pairing; over a member of it the preimage of `1` is a finite sum of pure tensors, which is
the dual basis fed to `tmul_comm_of_dualBasis`. -/
theorem hasLocallySymmetricSquare_of_isInvertible
    [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
    (L : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪))
    [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible 𝒪 h𝒪 L] :
    HasLocallySymmetricSquare 𝒪 J L.val := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨Lp, hLp, rfl⟩ : ∃ (Lp : PresheafOfModules.{w} (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
      (hLp : Presheaf.IsSheaf J Lp.presheaf),
      L = (⟨Lp, hLp⟩ : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)) :=
    ⟨L.val, L.isSheaf, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨Np, ψ, hsurj, hinj⟩ :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_locallyBijective_pairing (hO := h𝒪) hLp inferInstance
  have := hsurj
  have := hinj
  intro U
  refine ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.imgSieve
    (A := SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)) ψ (1 : 𝒪.obj (op U)), ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ψ) _
  · intro Y f hf
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := hf
    obtain ⟨n, x, y, hxy⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_fin_tmul_eq t
    have hxy' : (∑ j, x j ⊗ₜ y j : (Lp ⊗ Np).obj (op Y)) = t := hxy
    have hms : pairHom ψ (op Y) (∑ j, x j ⊗ₜ y j : (Lp ⊗ Np).obj (op Y))
        = ∑ j, pairHom ψ (op Y) (x j ⊗ₜ y j) := map_sum _ _ _
    have hsum : ∑ j, pairHom ψ (op Y) (x j ⊗ₜ y j) = 1 :=
      hms.symm.trans ((congrArg (fun z ↦ pairHom ψ (op Y) z) hxy').trans
        (ht.trans (PresheafOfModules.unit_map_one _ _)))
    exact tmul_comm_of_dualBasis hLp ψ (op Y) x y hsum

/-! ### Sheafification kills the self-braiding -/

section Sheafify

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules

/-- Over an object whose module of sections has symmetric tensor square, the self-braiding of a
presheaf of modules is the identity: the braiding of presheaves of modules is sectionwise the
transposition of a tensor square. -/
theorem braiding_app_eq_id (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (h : ∀ a b : P.obj U, a ⊗ₜ[(structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U] b
      = b ⊗ₜ[(structureRingPresheaf 𝒪).obj U] a) :
    (β_ P P).hom.app U = 𝟙 ((P ⊗ P).obj U) := by
  exact braiding_eq_id_of_tmul_comm (P.obj U) h

/-- **The self-braiding of a locally symmetric presheaf of modules is the identity after the
sheafification unit.** The two composites agree on a covering sieve of every object and the
target is a sheaf, hence separated. The braiding itself is in general *not* the identity before
sheafifying: the sections of an invertible sheaf of modules over an object which does not carry a
dual basis need not have symmetric tensor square. -/
theorem braiding_comp_toSheafify [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
    (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
    (P : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.{w} 𝒪) (hP : HasLocallySymmetricSquare 𝒪 J P) :
    (β_ P P).hom ≫ toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P) = toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P) := by
  refine PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun U ↦ ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hsym⟩ := hP U.unop
  refine Stacks.SheafRankOne.isSeparated_val 𝒪 h𝒪 ((sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).obj (P ⊗ P))
    U.unop S hS _ _ fun Y f hf ↦ ?_
  have key : (P ⊗ P).map f.op ((β_ P P).hom.app U x) = (P ⊗ P).map f.op x := by
    rw [← PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (β_ P P).hom f.op x,
      braiding_app_eq_id P (op Y) (hsym f hf)]
    rfl
  have h1 := (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P)) f.op
    ((β_ P P).hom.app U x)).symm
  have h2 := PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P)) f.op x
  exact h1.trans ((congrArg (fun z ↦ (toSheafify 𝒪 h𝒪 (P ⊗ P)).app (op Y) z) key).trans h2)

end Sheafify

/-! ### The self-braiding of an invertible sheaf of modules -/

section SheafBraiding

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory

variable [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **A sheaf of modules with locally symmetric tensor square has trivial self-braiding.** The
braiding on `SheafOfModules` is the localized braiding, so on the sheafification of a presheaf of
modules it is the braiding upstairs conjugated by the monoidality isomorphism; and a sheaf of
modules is isomorphic to the sheafification of its own underlying presheaf. -/
theorem braiding_eq_id_of_locallySymmetric
    (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
    (L : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪))
    (hL : HasLocallySymmetricSquare 𝒪 J L.val) : (β_ L L).hom = 𝟙 (L ⊗ L) :=
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.braiding_eq_id_of_iso
    ((Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyCounitIso 𝒪 h𝒪).app L).symm
    (Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.braiding_eq_id_of_localization (sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪)
      (Stacks.SheafInternalHom.localIso 𝒪 h𝒪) (Iso.refl _) L.val
      ((Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.map_eq_of_unit_comp_eq (sheafifyAdjunction 𝒪 h𝒪)
          (β_ L.val L.val).hom (𝟙 (L.val ⊗ L.val))
          ((braiding_comp_toSheafify h𝒪 L.val hL).trans (id_comp _).symm)).trans
        ((sheafify 𝒪 h𝒪).map_id _)))

/-- **An invertible sheaf of modules on an arbitrary site has trivial self-braiding**: the
braiding `β_ L L` is the identity. This is the hypothesis that the coherence of the canonical
multiplication on the tensor powers of an invertible sheaf of modules, Stacks Tag 01CU, requires;
see the module docstring for why it is not a formal consequence of the symmetric monoidal axioms.

Invertibility is taken in the spelling the tensor powers use,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`, and converted to the one the pairing comes from
by `Stacks.InvertiblePullback.stacksIsInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometryIsInvertible`. -/
instance hasTrivialSelfBraiding
    (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J (structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
    (L : SheafOfModules.{w} (structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible 𝒪 h𝒪 L] :
    Stacks.GradedSections.HasTrivialSelfBraiding L := by
  have : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible 𝒪 h𝒪 L :=
    (Stacks.InvertiblePullback.stacksIsInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometryIsInvertible
      𝒪 h𝒪 L).mpr inferInstance
  exact ⟨braiding_eq_id_of_locallySymmetric h𝒪 L
    (hasLocallySymmetricSquare_of_isInvertible h𝒪 L)⟩

end SheafBraiding

end Stacks.SelfBraidingInvertible

end
